Educational Disclaimer:
OrbitDesk is an independent educational training simulator. NOT affiliated with,
endorsed by, or connected to Influx, Microsoft, or any client. All clients
(NovaTech Enterprises, Bloom & Co Studio, Apex Financial Group) and agents
(Alex, Priya, Jamal, Lisa, David) are fictional personas. All tickets, logs,
policies, voice calls are simulated. Error codes (53000, 0x80180024, etc.) are
real Microsoft codes used under fair use for education. Voice samples are
synthetic (Web Speech API + generated MP3) for training purposes. No real
remote access, no real calls, no real tenant data. Runs 100% in browser
(LocalStorage), no tracking, no real data collection. All trademarks belong
to their respective owners.

Security:
- No hardcoded secrets, PATs, or API keys in code
- All simulated data, no real Microsoft connections
- Security headers: CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options
- Audit logs, RBAC, Break Glass, Zero Trust, Compliance per-client
- See SECURITY.md and THREAT_MODEL.md for full security policy

Desktop:
- PWA manifest + Service Worker for installable offline app
- Electron 28 wrapper for native desktop app (Windows .exe, macOS .dmg, Linux .AppImage)
- Build: npm run desktop:dist — Output in dist/ folder
- PWA install: Click Install in browser — No build needed, feels native

Voices:
- 5 balanced voices (men & women) with different personas
- Web Speech API speechSynthesis + speechRecognition + 9 MP3 pre-recorded samples
- Different voice per client: NovaTech male formal, Bloom female friendly, Apex male deep
- Tech experts: Alex male formal, Priya female friendly, David male deep
- Flowing conversations: Client talks, you respond, client does action, asks question, expert joins
